DECISIONS 340, CODEGEN.md §3.5: a go types emit declares Decode<Fn>File of a @text fn of a map or list after the records' decoders; the record RaritiesFile's Decode<T> is already DecodeRaritiesFile, so fn rarities meets it: E8005 at the fn.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// A rarity.
enum Rarity { common, rare }

/// The rarities file, as a record.
record RaritiesFile {
  /// The counts.
  counts: {Rarity: Int}
}

/// How many of each rarity.
@text("rarities.json")
export fn rarities() -> {Rarity: Int} { return { common: 1, rare: 2 } }

emit go { out: "@features/a/go", package: "a", mode: types }
emit text { out: "out/a" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  a/a.canon:15:11
  go: DecodeRaritiesFile is generated for both a.RaritiesFile and a.rarities

